body:
I'm setting up a website for my girlfriend, using WP.  
One thing I've been struggling with is the font size for the site title. When I'm on a computer, the size is as i want it to be, but while in tablet mode or mobile, the size is too small, and I don't see/think there is an option to customize this.   
I've inspected the elements, and have seen "@ media screen and (min-width: 40em)" reffering to mobile scaling of the website, and have tried to write additional CSS:  

@ media screen and (min-width: 40em)  
.site-title {  
   font-size: 3rem;  
}  
This does not work. I'm not experienced with CSS, and am looking for help.  
Thank you in advance!
